 <Worksheet ss:Name="TestPlan">
  <Table ss:DefaultColumnWidth="120" ss:DefaultRowHeight="15">
   <Column ss:Index="1" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="50"/>
   <Column ss:Index="2" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="90"/>
   <Column ss:Index="3" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="160"/>
   <Column ss:Index="4" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="5" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="400"/>
   <Column ss:Index="6" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="400"/>
   <Column ss:Index="7" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="8" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="9" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="10" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="80"/>
   <Column ss:Index="11" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="80"/>
   <Column ss:Index="12" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Row ss:Height="30">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Index</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">SS/Module</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Testcase Name</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Feature</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Steps</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Impacted Registers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Validation/Acceptance Criteria</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Speed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Mode</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Remarks</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:Height="200">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">Register Read/Write Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase validates the GPIO register block through two phases. Phase 1 (Reset Value Check): After hardware reset, each GPIO register is read and compared against its expected default value. Bit 0 (data_in, a read-only input pin level field) is masked out during comparison since its value depends on external pin state. Registers flagged in the reset-skip array or with no readable fields are skipped. Phase 2 (Write-Read Check): Six predefined data patterns are sequentially written to all writable GPIO registers. After each write pass, every register is read back and the result is compared against an expected value that accounts for read-only and write-only field behaviors — non-writable bits are expected to retain their default values while writable bits reflect the written pattern. Registers flagged in the skip array or with no writable/readable fields are excluded. The test passes only if both phases complete with zero mismatches across all registers including gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, and gp0_gpio_10.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Apply hardware reset (hreset_n) to the GPIO register block to initialize all registers to their default states.&#10;2. Read each GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10, and all remaining registers in the block) and mask out the data_in field (bit 0) since it reflects external pin state.&#10;3. Compare each masked read value against the expected default value for that register. Skip registers that are flagged for reset-skip or have no readable fields.&#10;4. Record any default value mismatches as failures.&#10;5. For each of the six test patterns (all-ones, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), write the pattern (masked by the write mask) to all writable GPIO registers. Skip registers flagged in the skip array or with no writable fields.&#10;6. After each write pass, read back every register (masked by the read mask) and compare against the expected value, which accounts for writable bits reflecting the written pattern and non-writable bits retaining their default values.&#10;7. Record any write-read mismatches as failures.&#10;8. Verify that both the default-value check and the write-read check complete with zero failures. The test passes only if all comparisons succeed across all registers and all patterns.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. All GPIO registers must return their expected default values after hardware reset (with bit 0 masked out for data_in field comparison). 2. For each of the six test data patterns, all writable register fields must reflect the written value when read back, while read-only and write-only fields must retain their default values. 3. The test must complete with zero default-value mismatches and zero write-read mismatches to pass. 4. Any single mismatch in either phase constitutes a test failure.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">Bit 0 (data_in) is masked out during default value comparison because it is a read-only field reflecting the external GPIO pin level, which may not match the register default. The io_ctrl field has a default value of 1 (input mode) while all other fields default to 0. Six complementary test patterns are used to exercise all bit positions. Registers at certain offsets are skipped during write-read checks (skip_array) and reset checks (skip_rst_array) as defined in the test configuration. The soft reset check function is disabled (dead code) and excluded from execution.</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
  <WorksheetOptions xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:excel">
   <FreezePanes/>
   <FrozenNoSplit/>
   <SplitHorizontal>1</SplitHorizontal>
   <TopRowBottomPane>1</TopRowBottomPane>
   <ActivePane>2</ActivePane>
  </WorksheetOptions>
 </Worksheet>
 <Worksheet ss:Name="MetaData">
  <Table ss:DefaultColumnWidth="150" ss:DefaultRowHeight="15">
   <Column ss:Index="1" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="50"/>
   <Column ss:Index="2" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="90"/>
   <Column ss:Index="3" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="160"/>
   <Column ss:Index="4" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="5" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="6" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="7" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="8" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="500"/>
   <Column ss:Index="9" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="10" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="11" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="12" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="13" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="80"/>
   <Column ss:Index="14" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="80"/>
   <Column ss:Index="15" ss:AutoFitWidth="1" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Row ss:Height="30">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Index</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">SS/Module</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Testcase Name</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Feature</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Test Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Test Steps</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Steps</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Meta Impacted Registers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Impacted Registers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Validation/Acceptance Criteria</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Speed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Mode</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="MetaHeader"><Data ss:Type="String">Remarks</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:Height="200">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">Register Read/Write Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase validates the GPIO register block by performing two main checks: (1) chk_rst_val() — iterates over all registers in addr_array[] (indexed 0 to CNT-1 where CNT=49) using MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10 (and remaining registers). For each register, it skips if skip_rst_array[i]==1 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, then calls read_reg(addr), masks the read data with 0xfffffffe (masking out bit 0 — the data_in RO field), and compares against default_value_array[i]. Mismatches increment def_fail_cnt. (2) chk_rd_wr() — iterates over 6 test patterns {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}. For each pattern, it writes (data_wr and write_mask_array[i]) to each register via write_reg(addr, ...), skipping if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000. Then reads back via read_reg(addr) masked with read_mask_array[i], computes expected value as ((data_wr and read_mask_array[i] and write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n and read_mask_array[i] and default_value_array[i])) where wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff), and compares. Mismatches increment wr_fail_cnt. The test calls finish(1) if any failure counter is non-zero, otherwise finish(0). The soft_reset_chk() function is dead code (#ifdef 0) and uses SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS which is ignored. The commented-out line write_reg(0xA0243ffc,0x12345678) is inactive. Header includes: gpio/gpio_def.h, gpio/gpio_offset.h. Base address resolved to 0xA001A000 via #define GPIO0 1 selecting MIZAR_GPIO_BASE = 0xA001A000. Each register (gp0_gpio_8/9/10) contains fields: data_in[0] RO, intr_raw_sts[1] RO, intr_clr[16] WO, pedge_intr_en[17] RW, nedge_intr_en[18] RW, level_sel[19] RW, io_ctrl[20] RW2 reset=1, dout[21] RW2 reset=0.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">This testcase validates the GPIO register block through two phases. Phase 1 (Reset Value Check): After hardware reset, each GPIO register is read and compared against its expected default value. Bit 0 (data_in, a read-only input pin level field) is masked out during comparison since its value depends on external pin state. Registers flagged in the reset-skip array or with no readable fields are skipped. Phase 2 (Write-Read Check): Six predefined data patterns are sequentially written to all writable GPIO registers. After each write pass, every register is read back and the result is compared against an expected value that accounts for read-only and write-only field behaviors — non-writable bits are expected to retain their default values while writable bits reflect the written pattern. Registers flagged in the skip array or with no writable/readable fields are excluded. The test passes only if both phases complete with zero mismatches across all registers including gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, and gp0_gpio_10.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Entry: test_case() is called.&#10;2. Call chk_rst_val():&#10;   a. Loop i from 0 to CNT-1 (CNT=49).&#10;   b. addr = addr_array[i] (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 at i=0, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9 at i=1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10 at i=2, etc.).&#10;   c. If skip_rst_array[i] == 1, skip (continue).&#10;   d. If read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, skip (continue).&#10;   e. data_rd = read_reg(addr).&#10;   f. data = (data_rd and 0xfffffffe) — mask out bit 0 (data_in field).&#10;   g. Compare data against default_value_array[i].&#10;   h. If mismatch: def_fail_cnt++, print failure with address, expected, and read values.&#10;   i. If match: print pass (under DEBUG_DISPLAY).&#10;3. Call chk_rd_wr():&#10;   a. Define chk_val[6] = {0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0xf5f5f5f5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000}.&#10;   b. Outer loop j from 0 to 5 (6 patterns).&#10;   c. data_wr = chk_val[j].&#10;   d. Write pass: Loop i from 0 to CNT-1.&#10;      i. addr = addr_array[i].&#10;      ii. If skip_array[i] == 1, skip.&#10;      iii. If write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, skip.&#10;      iv. write_reg(addr, (data_wr and write_mask_array[i])).&#10;   e. Read-back pass: Loop i from 0 to CNT-1.&#10;      i. addr = addr_array[i].&#10;      ii. If skip_array[i] == 1, skip.&#10;      iii. If write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, skip.&#10;      iv. If read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000, skip.&#10;      v. data_rd = (read_reg(addr) and read_mask_array[i]).&#10;      vi. wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xffffffff).&#10;      vii. exp_val = ((data_wr and read_mask_array[i] and write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n and read_mask_array[i] and default_value_array[i])).&#10;      viii. Compare data_rd against exp_val.&#10;      ix. If mismatch: wr_fail_cnt++, print failure.&#10;      x. If match: print pass (under DEBUG_DISPLAY).&#10;4. Check results: if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) then finish(1) else finish(0).&#10;5. soft_reset_chk() is dead code (#ifdef 0) — not executed. SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS ignored.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Apply hardware reset (hreset_n) to the GPIO register block to initialize all registers to their default states.&#10;2. Read each GPIO register (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10, and all remaining registers in the block) and mask out the data_in field (bit 0) since it reflects external pin state.&#10;3. Compare each masked read value against the expected default value for that register. Skip registers that are flagged for reset-skip or have no readable fields.&#10;4. Record any default value mismatches as failures.&#10;5. For each of the six test patterns (all-ones, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), write the pattern (masked by the write mask) to all writable GPIO registers. Skip registers flagged in the skip array or with no writable fields.&#10;6. After each write pass, read back every register (masked by the read mask) and compare against the expected value, which accounts for writable bits reflecting the written pattern and non-writable bits retaining their default values.&#10;7. Record any write-read mismatches as failures.&#10;8. Verify that both the default-value check and the write-read check complete with zero failures. The test passes only if all comparisons succeed across all registers and all patterns.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">1. All GPIO registers must return their expected default values after hardware reset (with bit 0 masked out for data_in field comparison). 2. For each of the six test data patterns, all writable register fields must reflect the written value when read back, while read-only and write-only fields must retain their default values. 3. The test must complete with zero default-value mismatches and zero write-read mismatches to pass. 4. Any single mismatch in either phase constitutes a test failure.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="DataCell"><Data ss:Type="String">Bit 0 (data_in) is masked out during default value comparison because it is a read-only field reflecting the external GPIO pin level, which may not match the register default. The io_ctrl field has a default value of 1 (input mode) while all other fields default to 0. Six complementary test patterns are used to exercise all bit positions. Registers at certain offsets are skipped during write-read checks (skip_array) and reset checks (skip_rst_array) as defined in the test configuration. The soft reset check function is disabled (dead code) and excluded from execution.</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
